WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:04.792
EXISTS asks only whether the inner query returns at least one row.

00:00:04.792 --> 00:00:09.692
The actual selected value inside the subquery usually does not matter.

00:00:09.692 --> 00:00:13.067
That is why SELECT one is common.

00:00:13.067 --> 00:00:18.642
The business meaning is simply: does any related row satisfy this condition?

00:00:18.642 --> 00:00:23.427
This makes EXISTS especially natural for relationship checks.

00:00:23.427 --> 00:00:29.077
EXISTS asks whether at least one related row satisfies the condition.

00:00:29.077 --> 00:00:35.817
The selected columns inside EXISTS usually do not matter; the existence of a row does.

00:00:35.817 --> 00:00:42.627
This maps naturally to questions such as patients with any follow-up, customers with any purchase,

00:00:42.627 --> 00:00:44.720
or orders with no shipment record.
